                <pb facs="0539" n="1293" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg1293"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111Sp1/24</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-31T14:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 31, 1917, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 1, 11.20
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>714. German submarine <hi rendition="#italic">B–23</hi> entered Corunna July 29,
                    3 p.m. British and Guatemalan Consuls telegraphed Captain General at Ferrol
                    requesting internment. He replied ordering submarine to Ferrol where it will be
                    interned until close of war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
